# .dockerignore — keeps the Docker build context lean and reproducible.
# Anything matched here is NOT sent to the Docker daemon, so it can't accidentally
# end up in the final image even if the Dockerfile says `COPY . .`.
# Pair this with the Dockerfile multi-stage copy — the `runtime` stage is also
# defensive about what it pulls from the builder.

# ─── VCS, IDE, and Replit metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Source-of-truth lives in the registry; .git/ is huge and untrusted at build.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
# Visual Studio solution cache (revit-addin). ~264MB of local IDE state.
.vs
.replit
replit.nix
replit.md

# ─── Local agent / Claude state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/ holds local IDE state, scheduled-tasks lockfiles, settings.local.json
# with developer-specific permissions. Never goes into a production image.
.claude

# ─── Reference repo (NOT a submodule) ───────────────────────────────────────
# MasterMiawW is a sibling chatbot reference (see memory note); it has its own
# .git/ and unrelated dependencies. Excluding saves ~hundreds of MB of context.
MasterMiawW

# ─── node_modules at every depth ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm install` runs INSIDE the builder stage; shipping a host node_modules
# would pollute the cache with OS-specific binaries (esbuild, sharp, etc.).
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ─── Build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ is regenerated by `pnpm run build`. Shipping a host-built dist/ would
# bypass the deterministic CI build and risk shipping uncommitted changes.
dist
**/dist
# apex pre-render output (ADR-055 §0 + scripts/build/prerender-apex.mjs).
# Cloudflare Pages serves this; the Fly image must never contain it.
**/dist-apex
build
**/build
# EXCEPTION: scripts/build/ is SOURCE, not build OUTPUT — it holds
# write-prod-shim.mjs (run at the END of `pnpm run build:docker`) and
# prerender-apex.mjs. The broad `**/build` above otherwise excludes it and breaks
# the Docker build with: Error: Cannot find module '/app/scripts/build/write-prod-shim.mjs'.
!scripts/build
!scripts/build/**
**/.next
**/.astro
.vite-cache
.turbo

# ─── Tests (NOT needed at runtime) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Test fixtures + snapshots are >50MB combined and never executed in prod.
# BUT: 8 tests/* dirs are pnpm WORKSPACE members (pnpm-workspace.yaml), so their
# package.json manifests MUST reach the builder or `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# fails with an outdated-lockfile error (the lockfile has importers for them).
# Strip the test SOURCE but keep the workspace manifests. The Dockerfile copies
# `tests` before install to satisfy workspace resolution; the source stays out.
tests
!tests/*/package.json
**/__tests__
**/__snapshots__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
.playwright
test-results

# ─── Coverage + CI artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage
.nyc_output

# ─── Docs (heavy + irrelevant to the running server) ───────────────────────
# *.md files in source dirs are stripped except LICENSE (legal requirement).
# Note: we KEEP CLAUDE.md out as well — it's a dev guide, not runtime config.
**/*.md
!LICENSE
!LICENSE.md
# docs-site is a separate Astro app — out of scope for the editor image.
apps/docs-site
# bench app is dev-only perf harness; not needed at runtime.
apps/bench

# ─── Logs + tmp ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
.tmp
.local
.local-*
.replit-cache
.upm

# ─── Env + secrets (CRITICAL — never ship these) ────────────────────────────
# Real secrets come from Fly's `flyctl secrets set` at deploy time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
pryzm-selfhost/.secrets
pryzm-selfhost/.env

# ─── OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Heavy assets that aren't needed at build/runtime ───────────────────────
# `attached_assets/` is Claude chat-paste history (see .gitignore §H28).
# `screenshots/` is dev evidence, not served.
attached_assets
generated_assets
screenshots
*.iso
*.tar
*.zip
*.7z

# ─── TypeScript incremental cache ───────────────────────────────────────────
# tsbuildinfo files leak host-absolute paths and confuse later incremental builds.
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── Docker self-reference ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Avoid re-copying the Dockerfile into the image (harmless, just noise).
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ─── First-deploy slim context (2026-06-03) ─────────────────────────────────
# These bloated the build-context upload to ~290MB (the transfer that aborted the
# first Fly deploy on a slow uplink). Excluded to ship a ~22MB context:
#  • public/items/ = ~185MB of GLB 3D-model catalog served at runtime. Baking
#    185MB of models into the image is an anti-pattern (ref §H28) — they belong
#    on object storage (Supabase Storage / CDN). TEMP TRADE-OFF: the in-app
#    furniture/items catalog GLBs 404 in prod until re-hosted; the core
#    onboarding→generate→edit pipeline is unaffected. Tracker: OBJECT-STORAGE-GLB.
#  • docs/ — markdown, not a build/runtime input.
#  • client/ — legacy (13 files; not referenced by the build/runtime).
#  • .agents/ — local agent scratch.
public/items
docs
client
.agents

# ─── Probe caches + research outputs (2026-08-06) ───────────────────────────
# The build context had grown to 2.8GB, dominated by UNTRACKED probe artefacts
# under tools/. `tools/` IS copied into the runtime image (Dockerfile L60/L178),
# so these are excluded surgically — each was verified to be referenced ONLY in
# source COMMENTS (provenance citations for measured constants), never read at
# runtime by server.js or any package:
#  • **/.cache          — 1.57GB, tools/cold-start-probe/.cache (untracked HTTP
#                         cache for the Spanish cadastre/planning probes).
#  • cordoba-ar-georef/out — 738MB of AR georeferencing probe output (3 tracked
#                         files); research evidence, not a build/runtime input.
#  • scratchpad/        — 34MB of one-off probe scripts (probe-l58*.mts). Cited
#                         in comments in site-parcel-data; never imported.
# Net effect: context 2.8GB → ~200MB, which is what makes a non-CI deploy path
# viable at all. Keep tools/<pack>/out for the small rule-pack probes — only the
# two heavy dirs above are excluded.
**/.cache
tools/cordoba-ar-georef/out
scratchpad
# The remaining per-probe out/ dirs (~24MB): rule-pack research evidence written
# by the tools/* probes. Verified 2026-08-06: ZERO runtime imports or file reads
# of any `tools/` path across server.js, server/, packages/*/src, apps/*/src —
# the only mentions are provenance comments. Excluded so the manual (non-CI)
# deploy path has a context small enough to upload over a domestic uplink.
tools/*/out

# ─── Context bloat found 2026-09-07 (manual deploy at 142 MB and climbing) ──
# The founder waits on every one of these deploys, and the context upload was
# taking >12 minutes before the build even started. Four directories slipped
# through the patterns above — each verified NOT to be a build or runtime input
# before being excluded here, because a wrong entry breaks the image silently:
#  • audit/ (56 MB, 1323 tracked files) — accessibility/architecture research
#    evidence. NOT a pnpm workspace member (pnpm-workspace.yaml globs are
#    packages/tools/apps/plugins/tests-only) and holds no package.json. The one
#    "audit" string in package.json is `@pryzm/wcag-audit`, which lives under
#    packages/ and is unaffected.
#  • public/apex/ (43 MB) — hero.mp4 / hero-hevc.mp4 / poster art for the APEX
#    marketing site. C51 §3.2.1: apex marketing paths are 301-REDIRECTED by
#    server.js:5937 to pryzm.so, never served from this image. Same rationale as
#    the existing `**/dist-apex` line — Cloudflare serves it, Fly must not carry
#    it. (`public/items` is already excluded above for the same class of reason.)
#  • lane4e-dist/ (36 MB) — a stale lane build artefact; ZERO references in the
#    Dockerfile, package.json, or any source.
#  • dist-server-deps/ (20 MB) — UNTRACKED host build output. The Dockerfile
#    mentions it only in a comment (:190); the bundles are produced inside the
#    builder stage. Shipping a host copy is exactly what the `dist` exclusions
#    above exist to prevent.
# ⚠ If a deploy ever fails with a missing path from one of these, the fix is to
# name that path with a `!` exception — not to delete the whole entry.
audit
public/apex
lane4e-dist
dist-server-deps
